course: dictionary
lesson: 8295
title: Rival: one word, three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rival is a person, team or business that competes with another for the same thing. Look at the clues: «The two schools are old rivals.» Old and two tell you this is a long contest between the same two schools.
explain: Rival can also be a verb meaning to be as good as someone or something: «Her cake rivals any shop's cake.» The cake is not fighting anyone. It is just as good as a shop cake. As an adjective, rival describes things that compete, like «rival teams» or «rival shops».
explain: Check the words around rival to find its job. If the sentence is about people or groups competing, it is a noun or adjective. If something is said to be as good as another thing, it is a verb. Then swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A rival is someone or something that competes with another for the same thing.
fact: «Rival» can be a noun, a verb or an adjective, so check the words around it to find its job.
fact: As a verb, «rival» means to be as good as: «Her cake rivals any shop's cake.»
fact: The male stag beetle uses its huge jaws to wrestle rivals, lifting and flipping them.
fact: A silverback gorilla beats his chest so rivals hear how big he is, and often a real fight is not needed.
exercise: «The two schools are old rivals.» In this sentence, what is a rival? | *A person, team or group that competes with another for the same thing | A teacher who is very kind | A school that is far away | A prize given at the end of term
exercise: «Her cake rivals any shop's cake.» What does rivals mean here? | Says sorry to | *Is just as good as | Hides from | Gives a prize to
exercise: «Rival shops offer different prices so people can compare them.» What does rival describe? | Colourful | Friendly | Tired | *Competing
test: «Old rivals from the game, such as France, Spain, Portugal and Italy, now work together.» What does rivals mean here? | Shops that sell cakes | *Teams or countries that used to compete | Friends who never argue | Players who sleep
test: «The male stag beetle's huge jaws look like a deer's antlers, and males use them to wrestle rivals.» What does rivals mean here? | Gentle friends | A kind of big tree | Very small grubs | *Other males competing for food or mates
exam: «After the Second World War the USA and the Soviet Union became rivals in the Cold War, and they raced to be first in space.» Which word best matches rivals? | Helpers | Neighbours | *Competitors | Visitors
